{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794324408,"nonce":"q39BYIdhneW2mwq4tGawcCqJ4RY=","title":"haxe_conformance: the wasm module cache ignores the build environment","message":"wasm_module_for reuses a module that is newer than its bytecode, ash and the runtime object. A switch like ASH_WASM_DIRECT changes the module without touching any of those, so a second arm run with a different ASH_* setting can be handed the first one's module and report its result as its own. The harness recompiles unit.hl on every run, which hides this unless --skip-build is given; found while checking that a run with the direct wasm backend really used it. Fix: the ASH_* environment the build ran under is stored beside the module (\u003cmodule\u003e.env) and a different set counts as stale. Checked with --skip-build: same env reuses, a changed env rebuilds.","files":null}]}